# Best Practices for AI Engineering

## Version Control and Configuration Management
- Use version control for prompts, models, and code
- Maintain a prompt template library
- Record model versions and configurations
- Use configuration management to track changes
- Implement semantic versioning
- Maintain a changelog for each version
- Use a branching strategy to isolate experimental changes
- Implement a code review process

## Monitoring and Observability
- Implement agent behavior logging
- Track key performance indicators (latency, success rate)
- Set up alerts for abnormal behavior
- Monitor resource usage and costs
- Visualize agent decision-making processes
- Implement distributed tracing
- Monitor model calls and dependent services
- Build dashboards for key metrics

## Continuous Integration and Deployment
- Build an automated test pipeline
- Implement a gradual rollout strategy
- Use A/B testing to evaluate changes
- Maintain fast rollback capabilities
- Automate deployment and infrastructure management
- Use environment separation (development, test, production)
- Implement code quality checks
- Automated documentation generation

## Feature Flags
- Use feature switches to control proxy functions
- Implement canary deployment
- Enable specific features for different user groups
- Roll out new features gradually to reduce risks
- Use A/B testing to evaluate new features
- Implement monitoring and metrics for feature switches
- Establish feature lifecycle management
- Automate feature switch management

## Scalability design
- Design an architecture that supports horizontal scalability
- Implement caching strategies to reduce model calls
- Use asynchronous processing and queue management
- Implement load balancing and traffic distribution
- Design stateless components for easy scalability
- Optimize resource usage efficiency
- Implement current limiting and degradation strategies
- Consider multi-region deployment and geographic distribution

## Technical debt management
- Perform code refactoring regularly
- Maintain a technical debt list
- Balance new feature development with debt repayment
- Set code quality and coverage goals
- Record design decisions and trade-offs
- Continuously review and update dependencies
- Eliminate obsolete code and interfaces
- Implement code complexity monitoring

## Developer experience
- Provide a comprehensive development environment setup
- Simplify local testing and debugging processes
- Maintain clear API documentation
- Create code samples and tutorials
- Build an internal knowledge base and best practices
- Automate repetitive development tasks
- Provide helpful error messages and debugging information
- Organize code demonstrations and learning sessions

## Cost Management
- Implement cost tracking for model usage
- Optimization tips to reduce token consumption
- Set budgets and resource usage limits
- Monitor and predict cost trends
- Implement a tiered caching strategy
- Allocate resources based on task importance
- Regularly review cost-effectiveness
- Experiment with cost-effectiveness of different models and providers